		{
			dependencies: ["72DE02C58750DFA9"]
			description: [
				"Hold a &6Hammer&r and right-click a &6Crafting Table&r to obtain the core item of this mod—the &6Workbench&r."
				""
				"Any vanilla tool that is modified once in the &6Workbench&r becomes a Tetra tool, gaining Tetra-specific attributes and systems."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"{image:kubejs:textures/task/tetra_1.png width:180 height:100 align:1}"
				""
				"As shown above, the Workbench interface is divided into several sections:"
				""
				"&aGreen Area:&r Displays the tool’s overall stats. Hold Shift to view detailed descriptions of each attribute."
				""
				"&4Red Area:&r Shows the tool’s parts. Clicking a component will open the blue section for further interaction."
				""
				"&bBlue Area:&r Used to enchant, honing, upgrade, or replace the selected component from the red area."
				""
				"&5Purple Area:&r Used to switch the content displayed in the blue area."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: false
			id: "312A09022249980F"
			rewards: [{
				id: "524D750A2FB330D2"
				item: "lightmanscurrency:coin_iron"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "Familiarize Yourself with the Workbench"
			tasks: [{
				advancement: "tetra:upgrades/workbench"
				criterion: ""
				id: "115950E130CCDA28"
				type: "advancement"
			}]
			title: "Understand the Workbench, Master the Workbenc"
			x: -1.25d
			y: 19.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["72DE02C58750DFA9"]
			description: [
				"When you &e craft a Hammer for the first time&r, the system will grant you a &6Holographic Orb&r."
				""
				"The &6Holosphere&r is a comprehensive but not very intuitive manual."
				""
				"While holding it, you can &eright-click&r to project a dedicated interface that displays information about &etool types, components, and material properties&r."
				""
				"&3If you have previously obtained a Holosphere in another save, a progression detection bug may prevent you from receiving the system’s automatic reward. &r&cIn that case, please obtain a new one from the quest below. &r"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The Holosphere also has two &eupgrade slots&r. In later progression, it can be enhanced by installing an &eEye of Ende&r, allowing you to &dlocate ancient forging ruins underground&r."
				""
				"It can also be used to &esearch for ancient debris&r. When carried in the off-hand, if these structures are nearby and the direction indicator aligns with them, the HUD will display an orange ripple effect."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: false
			id: "4632D20D50741511"
