		{
			dependencies: ["312A09022249980F"]
			description: [
				"Tetra-fied tools can only be repaired using the &6Workbench&r."
				""
				"In essence, repairing is the &ereconstruction of individual components&r, so it will require &emultiple types of materials&r. You can view the required repair material in the &dRepair Cycle&r section at the bottom-left of the repair interface."
			]
			id: "5BA7E809A7B3037B"
			rewards: [{
				id: "3922CD1D0436EEED"
				item: "lightmanscurrency:coin_iron"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "Repairing"
			tasks: [{
				id: "6870823584208C2D"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "How to Repair"
			x: -1.25d
			y: 22.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["312A09022249980F"]
			description: [
				"Place a vanilla tool into the Workbench, and depending on its type, the &eavailable moddable components&r will be displayed. By selecting different components, you can &ecustomize the material of each part&r."
				""
				"Tools that you have been using since the early game can be continuously refined by upgrading key components, changing both their materials and part types, thereby altering their properties and functionality."
				""
				"Crafting high-tier components requires a &chigher-level hammer&r."
				""
				"Simply using high-tier materials will not automatically make your tools stronger—&ecareful and balanced combinations are far more important&r."
			]
			id: "47A7AEEFD24F1D7A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "4E5A51FF9BB20304"
				item: "lightmanscurrency:coin_iron"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "Customise parts"
			tasks: [{
				id: "72B2A6B7FD5FFB12"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "How to Modify Tools"
			x: -1.25d
			y: 21.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["312A09022249980F"]
			description: [
				"Tool upgrades in Tetra can be divided into two categories:"
				""
				"1. Enhancement through accumulated &6Hone&r during use"
				"2. Additional &6Modification&r upgrades"
				""
				"During usage, the tool accumulates overall Hone progress. When the Honing bar is full, a notification will appear in the top-right corner of the screen. At this point, you can go to the Workbench and select a component to perform a &6Honing Upgrade&r on its attributes."
				""
				"Each parts is treated as an independent component. Different parts can be &eenchanted&r separately, or &eremodified&r individually to further refine their performance."
			]
			id: "6F6EA56EB887392B"
			rewards: [{
				id: "07DD8167FBB671A0"
				item: "lightmanscurrency:coin_iron"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "Make it stronger"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1370A7D6D3F44CCC"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "How to Upgrade Tools"
			x: -1.25d
			y: 20.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6F6EA56EB887392B"]
			description: [
				"&dUsing the “Double Headed Tool” section as an example&r"
				""
				"The mining level of an &eDouble Headed Tool&r is determined by the &ehighest tier plus one level&r among its head components when they differ."
				""
				"&dExample:&r"
				"When the head section contains &eonly one Diamond Pickaxe component&r, the tool is treated as having the &eIron Pickaxe mining level (one tier above Diamond Pickaxe)&r."
				""
				"When both head components in the head section are &eDiamond Pickaxe components&r, the tool reaches the &eDiamond Pickaxe mining level&r."
			]
			id: "56C75C9FAD3CEC66"
			rewards: [{
				id: "54C886646E87D6C8"
				item: "lightmanscurrency:coin_iron"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "Many effects do not necessarily mean mastery."
			tasks: [{
				id: "0B6873F9FA299058"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Level of the Double Headed Tools"
			x: -2.25d
			y: 21.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4632D20D50741511"]
			description: [
				"The &dForge Ruins&r are the only naturally generated structures added by Tetra. They contain the Tetra &6Forge Hammer&r as well as various special items."
				""
				"The Forge Ruins come in two variants: one is the &6standard Forge Ruin&r, and the other is a &cForge Ruin containing a Core Extractor&r."
				""
				"You may need to take some devices and blocks from within the ruins, but note that only a &6Hammer enchanted with &bSilk Touch&r can fully preserve and collect them."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"These structures can generate in &eall biomes&r, most commonly within the &edeep slate layer&r. Testing shows that most ruins tend to generate near &eLush Caves&r, which themselves are frequently found underground beneath &espruce forests and jungles&r. Therefore, these two biome types are recommended as starting points when searching for ruins."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: false
			icon: "tetra:forged_workbench"
			id: "35E219B64C68FB53"
			rewards: [
				{
					count: 2
					id: "13423AA2EA03D680"
					item: "tetra:forged_bolt"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "330924A495EDD1CD"
					item: "lightmanscurrency:coin_iron"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			subtitle: "Advanced Modification Techniques"
			tasks: [{
				advancement: "tetra:spelunking/ancient_ruins"
				criterion: ""
				id: "6966D5E9CC42536C"
				title: "踏入锻造遗迹"
				type: "advancement"
			}]
			title: "Find the Ancient Forge Ruins"
			x: -1.25d
			y: 26.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6F6EA56EB887392B"]
			description: [
				"Setting aside the more intuitive stats such as &amining speed&r and &amining level&r—values already present in vanilla Minecraft—"
				""
				"the following will focus on the &especial stats introduced by the Tetra mod&r, which give tools their &eunique behaviors and advanced properties&r."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"After a vanilla tool is &emodified&r once in the &6Workbench&r, it gains a new attribute called &6Honing Value&r."
				""
				"By &eusing the tool for its intended function&r, its overall Honing value will gradually increase."
				""
				"When the Honing progress bar is full, the tool can be returned to the Workbench, where you may select one of its components to receive an &eupgrade attribute&r."
				""
				"These upgrade attributes themselves have &elimits&r, and selecting certain upgrades may consume &aIntegrity usage&r."
				""
				""
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"As each component is used over time, it gradually becomes &aSettle&r, eventually gaining the &e“Settled”&r property."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Setting aside the fact that upgrade attributes themselves have an &elevel cap&r, selecting a &aHoning Attribute Upgrade&r will consume &aIntegrity usage&r."
				""
				"&aIntegrity&r can be understood as the &elimit of components&r that a single tool can support."
				""
				"The &ematerial and type of each component&r will affect the tool’s overall integrity usage."
				""
				"You can &eremodify the modification section&r to expand a tool’s integrity, or adjust it by &echanging the materials of its components&r."
				""
				"At the same time, each component will gradually become &efixed&r through usage, eventually gaining the &a“Stable”&r property."
				""
				"Each level of &aSettled&r grants the tool additional &eintegrity usage&r."
			]
			id: "48BD60FBFEC2896A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "714D7A94A0CA67CB"
