		{
			dependencies: ["6F6EA56EB887392B"]
			description: [
				"Tetra-fied tools cannot be repaired or enchanted using an anvil, but they &ecan still be enchanted at an enchanting table&r."
				""
				"By placing the tool into the enchanting table, under ideal conditions, each component of the tool can receive &aenchantments&r."
				""
				"&aDisenchanting&r is also simple: replace the enchanted material of a component with another material to remove its enchantments."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Similarly, tools can also be enchanted using enchanted books."
				""
				"However, doing so consumes the tool’s &aMagic Capacity&r."
				""
				"The more magic capacity is consumed, the lower its value becomes. If it drops too low or becomes negative, &acurses&r are more likely to appear."
				""
				"Curses can be removed using lapis lazuli and experience levels."
			]
