		{
			dependencies: ["35E219B64C68FB53"]
			description: [
				"The &eThermal Cells&r installed on the &6Forge Hammer&r are consumable. If you do not want them to be single-use, you will need a &eCharging Device&r."
				""
				"{image:kubejs:textures/task/tetra_6.png width:150 height:102 align:1}"
				"As shown, a full charging setup consists of &6Extractor pipes&r, a &6Core Extractor&r, and a &6Transfer Unit&r combined into a single system."
				""
				"The &6Extractor Pipes&r must be placed above &6Seeping Bedrock&r. Do not worry, &6Seeping Bedrock&r can be found within &dForge Ruins equipped with Core Extractor components&r. (Multiple Extraction Pipes can be connected between the &6Core Extractor&r and the &6Seeping Bedrock&r to extend the system.)"
				""
				"It is important to note that the &6Transfer Unit&r must be placed on the &eprotruding face&r of the &6Core Extractor&r. After placing a &6Thermal Cell&r above the Transfer Unit, you must use a &eHammer&r to strike the switch on the Transfer Unit until it is set to the &ecentral position&r, thereby activating the charging process."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			id: "76BEE3F046554382"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2C21E23B468B23FD"
				item: "lightmanscurrency:coin_gold"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Device to charge the Thermal Cell"
			tasks: [{
				advancement: "tetra:spelunking/refill_cell"
				criterion: ""
				id: "208B3E22C248F072"
				type: "advancement"
			}]
			title: "Extract Enery from the Core！"
			x: 1.0d
			y: 27.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4632D20D50741511"]
			description: [
				"When searching for different biomes, you often need to check their generation rules one by one. However, in a modded environment with many additions, natural generation becomes highly complex and unpredictable. At this point, you may need the &2Nature Compass&r to assist in locating biomes or structures."
				""
				"By right-clicking the compass, you can use its search interface to specifically locate and search for the desired biome."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			icon: {
